From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:59:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: dsi2: Add missing sentinel to the RK3588 chip
 data

dw_mipi_dsi2_rockchip_probe() walks the chip data array until it finds
an entry whose .reg matches the controller base address or hits an
entry with .reg == 0. The RK3576 array is terminated that way, but the
RK3588 one is not, so a node whose address matches neither DSI host
makes the loop read past the end of rk3588_chip_data[] instead of
failing with "No dsi-config".

Add the sentinel. dsi0 and dsi1 as described in rk3588-base.dtsi match
before the end, so this does not change behaviour for them.

(Fixes: the commit that added the RK3588 DSI2 glue driver; this shallow
tree cannot resolve its hash.)

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw-mipi-dsi2-rockchip.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw-mipi-dsi2-rockchip.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw-mipi-dsi2-rockchip.c
index 6db886650..dd7e5f9b3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw-mipi-dsi2-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw-mipi-dsi2-rockchip.c
@@ -486,7 +486,8 @@ static const struct rockchip_dw_dsi2_chip_data rk3588_chip_data[] = {
 		.reg = 0xfde30000,
 		.grf_regs = rk3588_dsi1_grf_reg_fields,
 		.max_bit_rate_per_lane = 4500000ULL,
-	}
+	},
+	{ /* sentinel */ }
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id dw_mipi_dsi2_rockchip_dt_ids[] = {
